       title="JirAI: Remote Development and Architecture" id="JirAI-Remote-Development-and-Architecture">

    <primary-label ref="jirai"/>
    <secondary-label ref="jirai_version"/>

    <p>Understand JirAI's client-server architecture, Split Mode operation with JetBrains Gateway, and security principles.</p>

    <chapter title="Modular Client-Server Architecture" id="architecture">
        <p>JirAI is architected with complete modular separation to provide first-class support for JetBrains Remote Development and Split Mode:</p>
        <deflist>
            <def title="Jira.frontend">
                <p>Runs inside the JetBrains Client or local IDE. Hosts tool windows, dialogs, custom renderers, and the description editor. Never handles plaintext credentials.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Jira.backend">
                <p>Runs on the remote host (or backend IDE process). Manages network communication with Jira Cloud, reads from <code>PasswordSafe</code>, handles HTTP proxy authentication, and caches session data.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Jira.shared">
                <p>Contains serializable wire contracts and RPC interfaces connecting frontend and backend modules over the IntelliJ Platform RPC.</p>
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Split Mode Data Flow" id="data-flow">
        <list>
            <li><p><b>Authentication:</b> When you sign in via the JetBrains Client, the API token is sent securely across RPC to the host once, where it is stored in the host's <code>PasswordSafe</code>. It is never persisted on the client machine.</p></li>
            <li><p><b>Attachment Streaming:</b> Files selected on the client machine are streamed over RPC to the host for upload to Jira. Similarly, downloads stream from Jira through the host to the client file system.</p></li>
            <li><p><b>Proxy Settings:</b> Because all Jira API communication originates from the host process, the remote server's proxy configuration is utilized seamlessly.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Privacy and Zero Telemetry" id="privacy">
        <p>JirAI is built with strict privacy and security standards:</p>
        <list>
            <li><p><b>Zero Telemetry:</b> JirAI contains no tracking code, usage analytics, error submitters, or telemetry beacons.</p></li>
            <li><p><b>Strict Origin Enforcement:</b> Authenticated requests are strictly locked to your configured Jira Cloud domain (<code>*.atlassian.net</code>). The HTTP client strictly refuses any off-site redirect on authenticated routes.</p></li>
            <li><p><b>Third-Party Assets:</b> User avatars are loaded directly from Atlassian's CDN without transmitting authentication tokens.</p></li>
            <li><p><b>No Bundled External Dependencies:</b> Every runtime dependency is provided by the IntelliJ Platform itself, avoiding third-party dependency vulnerabilities.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

